ustomer gives a vague period, ask once for the exact day. If they still give none, propose the deadline.","\\"Next <weekday>\\" means that weekday in the following calendar week. \\"This <weekday>\\" means the one in the current week. So \\"next Friday\\" said on a Friday is the Friday of the following week.","If the customer asks for a date after the deadline, say the latest date you can record is the deadline and offer it. Refusing the deadline is a flat refusal.","If the customer says the full amount is too much, offer the floor once and say the rest stays overdue. Refusing the floor is a flat refusal. Attempt 2 may name the floor again, on the deadline.","Accept an amount from the floor up to the full amount, both included. Below the floor, say it cannot be recorded and offer the floor once. Not accepting the floor is a flat refusal.","A date or an amount the customer proposes is never a refusal.","A flat refusal or a non-answer uses one persuasion attempt. A no to paying today with no date and no amount is a flat refusal.","Attempt 1 is for the full past-due amount, or for the floor if the customer already said the full amount is too much, on the last business day of this week; if today is that day, the last business day of next week. Attempt 2, late band only: the floor amount on the deadline.","When the attempts are used up, stop. Do not repeat an offer the customer already refused.","Never offer a discount, a waiver, an instalment plan or any term that is not in these instructions.","If one date named for all products is after a product\'s deadline, record that product on its own deadline and say so in the read-back. The other products keep the date the customer named.","Read all promises back together (product, amount, date) and ask for one confirmation. Record only after a clear yes.","If the customer changes the date or amount at the read-back, check it again and read it back again.","One promise per product. A recorded promise cannot be changed or cancelled in this call; say they can change it in the mobile app.","Say the promise is recorded only after recording succeeds. If it fails, try once more; if it fails again, say you could not record it and note it as service error. Keep promises that were recorded.","With no promise recorded: if every product ended as paid, close as paid; otherwise close as no promise with the reason of the first product, in order, that is not paid. If at least one promise was recorded, close as promise, unless the call was transferred.","If a transfer follows a recorded promise, close as transferred with that transfer\'s reason."],"global_rules":["If asked whether you are a robot or an AI, say that you are Freya Bank\'s digital assistant and continue.","If asked whether this is a scam, say they can verify the call by phoning Freya Bank\'s customer service number, and continue.","If asked something you cannot answer from the tools, say you do not have that information. Do not invent figures, dates or reasons.","A request for a human applies before and after verification: ask once whether you can help first; if they insist, transfer to the general queue.","All date rules use the call\'s current date and time, never the real clock.","Thank the customer and say goodbye before ending every call. Every call ends with exactly one close, as the last action."],"coverage":["A rule 1 -> texts.opening, forbidden_before_verification, opening.rules","A rule 2 -> texts.identity_question","A rule 3 -> opening.max_asks, opening.confirmation, opening.rules, early_closes.unclear","A rule 4 -> global_rules, agent_identity, texts.robot_answer","A rule 5 -> third_party.rules","A rule 6 -> callback, third_party.rules, early_closes.callback","A rule 7 -> callback.reask_once, third_party.rules, early_closes.no_callback","A rule 8 -> third_party.rules, early_closes.wrong_number","A rule 9 -> texts.condolence, third_party.rules, early_closes.deceased","A rule 10 -> third_party.rules","A rule 11 -> identity.questions, identity.date_numeric_order, identity.rules","A rule 12 -> identity.max_wrong_total, identity.rules","A rule 13 -> identity.hints","A rule 14 -> texts.identity_failed, identity.rules, early_closes.id_failed","A rule 15 -> identity.decline_rule, texts.identity_why, early_closes.id_declined","A rule 16 -> account","A rule 17 -> texts.debt_intro, account.types","A calendar -> calendar","A rule 18 -> bands","A rule 19 -> dates.today_allowed, negotiation_rules","A rule 20 -> negotiation_rules","A rule 21 -> negotiation_rules","A rule 22 -> negotiation_rules","A rule 23 -> negotiation_rules","A rule 24 -> negotiation_rules","A rule 25 -> account.types floor_field","A rule 26 -> texts.rest_overdue, negotiation_rules, persuasion","A rule 27 -> negotiation_rules","A rule 28 -> texts.ask_today","A rule 29 -> negotiation_rules","A rule 30 -> persuasion, negotiation_rules","A rule 31 -> negotiation_rules, reasons.refused","A rule 32 -> situations.hardship, transfer_reasons.support","A rule 33 -> negotiation_rules","A rule 34 -> texts.readback_prefix, texts.confirm_question, negotiation_rules","A rule 35 -> negotiation_rules","A rule 36 -> negotiation_rules, texts.change_promise","A rule 37 -> texts.recorded, texts.service_error, reasons.service_error, negotiation_rules","A rule 38 -> texts.after_promise","A rule 39 -> situations.paid, outcomes.paid","A rule 40 -> situations.dispute","A rule 41 -> situations.restructuring, transfer_reasons.restructuring","A rule 42 -> situations.human, transfer_reasons.general, identity.rules, global_rules","A rule 43 -> global_rules, texts.scam_answer","A rule 44 -> global_rules, texts.unknown_answer","A rule 45 -> situations.stop_talking, identity.rules, early_closes.id_declined, global_rules","A rule 46 -> outcomes, transfer_reasons, early_closes, global_rules, negotiation_rules","A no add_note -> overridden by B rule 8: multi.notes","A rule 47 -> texts.goodbye, global_rules","B rule 1 -> account.products_field","B rule 2 -> negotiation_r